{
  "slug": "belmont",
  "name": "Belmont",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A toolkit for running structured coding sessions with AI coding agents. Belmont manages a PRD (Product Requirements Document), orchestrates specialized sub-agent phases, and tracks progress across milestones.\n\nA flexible PRD system has been used to provide the best level of context from plan to implementation. Tech plans allow you to specify specifics for the agent to follow while building.\n\nStrong guardrails are in place to keep the agent focused and on task.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **16 skills** and **6 agents**.\n\n- **Skills** (16): `cleanup` (Reduce input token bloat by archiving completed features, removing stale milestone files, trimming notes, and auditing convention files…), `codex-plan-apply` (Apply a Codex-only Belmont planning handoff packet after a plan-mode product-plan or tech-plan interview; write only the explicit…), `debug` (Debug router — choose between auto (agent-verified, narrow code fix) and manual (user-verified, deep spec context, in-place spec…), `debug-auto` (Auto debug loop — investigate, fix, verify using agent-dispatched pipeline), `debug-manual` (Manual debug loop with deep Belmont context and in-place spec reconciliation — user-verified fix + correct the specs…), `implement` (Implement the next pending milestone from the PRD using the agent pipeline), `loop` (Claude Code only), `next` (Implement just the next single pending task using the implementation agent), and 8 more\n- **Agents** (6): `code-review-agent`, `codebase-agent`, `design-agent`, `implementation-agent`, `reconciliation-agent`, `verification-agent`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install belmont@claude-community` from `blake-simpson/belmont` (`plugin`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 16,
    "agent": 6
  },
